<p>The United States announced a new round of sanctions targeting Iran’s oil trade, including a China-based independent refinery and about 40 shipping companies and tankers that Washington said were involved in transporting Iranian crude. The move is part of the Trump administration’s broader effort to cut off a key source of revenue for Iran by tightening pressure on what U.S. officials describe as Tehran’s shadow oil-export network. China responded by urging Washington to stop sanctioning Chinese companies. The new measures show the administration is widening pressure not just on Iranian sellers, but also on the foreign firms and vessels that help move those sales, extending U.S. enforcement beyond Iran itself.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/L8ZatibZVG1h8ChrnwLbWpmJllk6l9yPyvNErcf9uST0QfDpLnhN96xUS1d3snXjKyWuLPYuIpo2xo-HBp01htiZYX8HgrY8jARHTPP-NRo6tOfWNTed_67hBWby8FmUuUogC5y92uSOEqzaTflAaXBV8XwJrR23By3DvqRaWh9x7Snc' alt='Kharg Island, Iran’s main hub for oil exports, in 2017. The Trump administration broadened its effort to squeeze Iran’s oil industry on Friday with a range of sanctions.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Refinery target: The sanctions hit a Chinese &quot;teapot&quot; refinery, a term commonly used for smaller independent processors that have become important buyers of discounted crude outside the largest state-owned firms.</li><li>Secondary pressure: SCMP reported that the move follows the administration’s warning that it would impose secondary sanctions on companies and countries that continue doing business with Iran’s oil sector.</li><li>Revenue focus: The Treasury action centers on oil because exports remain Iran’s main external revenue source, making energy trade the clearest pressure point in U.S. sanctions policy.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: U.S. officials described the sanctions as part of a stepped-up campaign to cut Iran’s oil income and penalize foreign firms and vessels that help move that crude to market. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351389/us-sanctions-china-based-oil-refinery-and-40-shippers-over-iran-oil'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: Beijing called on Washington to stop using sanctions against Chinese companies, signaling its opposition to U.S. penalties on Chinese entities involved in the oil trade. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-imposes-sanctions-on-chinese-teapot-refinery-for-buying-iranian-oil'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-imposes-sanctions-on-china-based-oil-refinery-40-shippers-over-iranian-oil/article70904476.ece'>U.S. imposes sanctions on China-based oil refinery, 40 shippers over Iranian oil</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351389/us-sanctions-china-based-oil-refinery-and-40-shippers-over-iran-oil'>US sanctions China-based oil refinery and 40 shippers over Iran oil</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/25/mrfp-a25.html'>Hegseth says Iran blockade “going global,” as US announces new sanctions on Chinese shipping</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/24/world/middleeast/iran-sanctions-oil-tankers-shadow-fleet.html'>U.S. Unveils More Sanctions Targeting Iran’s Shadow Fleet</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-imposes-sanctions-on-chinese-teapot-refinery-for-buying-iranian-oil'>US imposes sanctions on Chinese ‘teapot’ refinery for buying Iranian oil</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>